# forge-managed
#
# Generated files. Prettier must not rewrite them.
#
# The vue hook runs `cd {{dir}} && npx prettier --write .` with
# pass_filenames: false, so `files:` decides whether the hook runs, not what it
# touches — prettier formats the whole of {{dir}}. Where a repo keeps its Vue
# app in a subdirectory that is harmless. Where the component sits at the repo
# root, prettier reaches the generated files: it reindents every `# generated:`
# marker in .pre-commit-config.yaml and requotes node-version in the CI
# workflow, and the generator rewrites them back on its next run. Two writers on
# one file have no fixed point, and the repo drifts on every run of either tool.
#
# Ownership decides, not formatting preference: these files are generated, and
# the generator is the only thing entitled to their shape.
#
# The generator adopts a deployed copy only while its entries match the
# template, so an entry swap lands only once every copy carries the marker
# above.
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.github/workflows/validate.yml
.markdownlint.json
.editorconfig
.golangci.yml
.sqlfluff
